     "parsed_output": null,
     "text": "Round 3 ran at 0.0216 ms. This round makes one change: the tile per block doubles from 4096 to 8192 elements. I have not measured whether it helps.\n\n- **Why it might help:** Each block moves twice as many bytes per load/store pair. That means more data in flight per block and half the block count (2560 instead of 5120).\n- **Why it doesn't hurt elsewhere:** Register use per tile stays modest, and the kernel structure is unchanged.\n- **Edge handling:** `n = 20971520` is an exact multiple of 8192, so the bounds-clipped store never actually has to drop any elements.\n\n```python title=\"impl_cutile.py\"\nimport torch\nimport cuda.tile as ct\n\nConstInt = ct.Constant[int]\n\n# Fixed configuration literals\n_TILE = 8192\n\n_CONFIG = {\"TILE\": _TILE}\n\n\n@ct.kernel\ndef _vector_add_kernel(x, y, out, TILE: ConstInt):\n    bid = ct.bid(0)\n    # Any out-of-bounds lanes of a partial last tile are dropped by the\n    # bounds-clipped store, so no padding value is needed.\n    a = ct.load(x, (bid,), (TILE,))\n    b = ct.load(y, (bid,), (TILE,))\n    ct.store(out, (bid,), a + b)\n\n\ndef run(x, y):\n    xf = x.view(-1)\n    yf = y.view(-1)\n    out = torch.empty_like(x)\n    of = out.view(-1)\n    n = xf.numel()\n    if n == 0:\n        return out\n    grid = (ct.cdiv(n, _TILE),)\n    ct.launch(torch.cuda.current_stream(), grid, _vector_add_kernel,\n              (xf, yf, of, _TILE))\n    return out\n\n\ndef get_last_config() -> dict:\n    return dict(_CONFIG)\n```",
